A||||3||Pyric||Hot trunk looking for scoop with nice curves.||||5||
Z||000000||Pyric||11-21-2001||06:16 PM||||Sorry... I couldn't think of a good subject line, so that will have to do.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"><P>Anyway, my trunk, like most, builds up a good amount of heat.  The last time it did so, it melted through the wire leading to the fuel pump.   <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>In trying to avoid future incidents like that, I was considering putting a scoop on the trunk.  Now I've read in several other threads that the ones that pop over the top of the roof don't work, but what about the ones that open backwards and just let air escape.  <P>My question is<BR>1. Does it help?<BR>2. which is the best one?<BR>and<BR>3. How much work is involved in installing it? (i.e. bondo/fiberglass bodywork)<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||11-21-2001||06:21 PM||||1)Yes, they work- hot air escapes through the opening.<P>2) Ferrari_MoMo just lowered the price on his in the mall to $60+SH (good deal)<P>3) They can be either bolted on or glassed in for a smoother look. As easy or as difficult as you want it to be!<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||11-21-2001||07:53 PM||||The ones that pop over the roof but hook up to the side vents don't work, But the Idy scoop that goes in the middle does work. The Mustang type scoop also works great for cooling. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Bazooka||11-21-2001||08:03 PM||||Pyro,    The rear decklid scoop is a good idea to allow warm air to escape from the engine compartment. I can actually feel the heat with my hand over the outlets after I shut the engine off. There is a wide variety of styles available. I removed my decklid, did the fiberglas work and had the paint shop match and finish it.<BR>*********************************<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.members.aol.com:/m34chev/snorkels.jpg">      <P>*********************************||||reg||1
